## 1. `describeCheckout` — Option Bag Junk Drawer (L10–19)

`option_bag_junk_drawer::src/petty.ts::describeCheckout`, confidence 0.74, agent_risk 0.39

> · parameter: options
> · 6 distinct property reads: currency, plan, region, retry, role, status

**What an agent gets wrong today.** The body is a positional `join(":")` — the output is a delimited key (cache key, telemetry id, dedupe token; nothing in the file says which). Six unrelated concerns arrive through one parameter: commercial (`plan`, `currency`), identity (`role`), geography (`region`), and attempt state (`status`, `retry`). An agent told to "add locale to checkout" adds `locale: string` to `CheckoutOptions` and has no signal whether `describeCheckout` must include it. Both outcomes are silent breakage: append it and every previously-emitted key changes shape; omit it and two distinct checkouts now collide on one key. `retry: boolean` is also flattened through `String()` into an untagged positional slot — reordering the array literal is invisible at the type level and changes every key the function has ever produced.

**Refactor.** Minimum viable — destructure exactly the fields the function owns, which is what kills the detector's "reads on a generic bag" signal:

```ts
export function describeCheckout({
  plan, role, region, currency, status, retry,
}: CheckoutOptions): string {
  return [plan, role, region, currency, status, String(retry)].join(":");
}
```

The version that actually protects the key format — split the bag into narrow records and make the ordering a declared constant instead of an array-literal accident:

```ts
export interface CheckoutIdentity { plan: string; role: string }
export interface CheckoutMarket   { region: string; currency: string }
export interface CheckoutAttempt  { status: string; retry: boolean }

/** Order is part of the emitted key. Appending changes every existing key. */
const CHECKOUT_KEY_ORDER = ["plan", "role", "region", "currency", "status", "retry"] as const;

export function describeCheckout(
  identity: CheckoutIdentity,
  market: CheckoutMarket,
  attempt: CheckoutAttempt,
): string {
  const parts: Record<(typeof CHECKOUT_KEY_ORDER)[number], string> = {
    plan: identity.plan,
    role: identity.role,
    region: market.region,
    currency: market.currency,
    status: attempt.status,
    retry: String(attempt.retry),
  };
  return CHECKOUT_KEY_ORDER.map((k) => parts[k]).join(":");
}
```

Now "add locale" forces a decision at three visible points — which record it belongs to, whether it enters `CHECKOUT_KEY_ORDER`, and the comment saying what happens if it does.

